  "prompt": "Compare two scenarios of SCOUT's high-rise shadow case on the Chicago Loop. Load SCOUT's Loop buildings from the Data Catalog; in one scenario keep them as they are, in the other, edit the buildings in an interaction node whose edit log takes out the 15 buildings SCOUT's second scenario removes, by their building ids, so more can be picked on its map and removed, raised or lowered later and the results after it updated. In both, turn the buildings' heights into a zoom 16 height raster with SCOUT's building rasterizer, run SCOUT's Deep Umbra shadow model on it, with one season setting both scenarios share, set to summer, and take apart what it returns: the accumulated shadow raster, and SCOUT's own mean and median accumulated shadow over the ground. In each scenario, also draw the buildings in 3D coloured by height, the height raster, and the accumulated shadow raster, each on its own Autark map. Then chart the two scenarios' mean accumulated shadow on a Vega-Lite pie chart that compares the scenarios, each slice in its scenario's colour with its value beside it, and take the absolute difference of the two scenarios' shadow rasters, cell by cell, with a raster calculator, drawn on its own Autark map in reds. The rasterizer and the shadow model are not part of the standard node set, so whatever provides them needs installing first.",
  "context": null,
