  "notes": "Two scenarios over a shared context; the Towers removed scenario's buildings come from an Interaction node (curio.builtin/edit-features) whose edit log removes the 15 building_ids, in place of WhatIfShadows' Data Transformation: SCOUT's buildings and a season Parameter node, SCOUT's rasterizer, the height mosaic, and Deep Umbra in each scenario, whose (shadow, metrics) two Python Computation nodes take apart, and three Autark maps in each (the buildings in 3D, the height raster and the shadow raster). The chart of SCOUT's mean is a Vega-Lite pie comparing the scenarios (its spec reads its inputs stacked, the dataset inputs, and names each circle's scenario from __input__), reading its stacked inputs, and the change in shadow is a Python node taking the absolute difference of the two shadow rasters (curio_raster_calculate(\"subtract\", [input_1, input_0], absolute=True)) with an Autark node mapping it."
